# How to run

This will parse `examples/Casino.java`, find the FSM state variable, find its FSM `G(F)`
parametrized with accepting states `F`, and then translate `G(s)` for each FSM state `s` to
μ-regular expressions and trace formulas:

```
cd app
gradle run --args="examples/Casino.java"
```

This prints latex commands defined in `app/commands_cats.tex`.

You can put in FSMs without Java code instead by passing a text file that lists all transitions,
starting state, and accepting states,
formatted like the text files in `examples/`.

```
gradle run --args="-fsm examples/csa4.txt"
```

(Text files `csa*.txt` are the suffix FSMs from the case study.)

If you want to print all `G(s)`, like in the Java example above, enter instead:

```
gradle run --args="-all -fsm <textfile>"
```
